#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "public-comment decide, or decide: code on GitHub from a login in config.json editors. accepted, accepted-modified, not-accepted, noted, deferred; a reason for all but accepted. Also reopens a decided comment."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/public-comment.bpmn:177
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "public-comment edit --branch: the author (human, or an agent in the author role) edits the folio's blocks as the decision says, on a feature branch for one change-set. Its PR says Closes #N for the change-set issue, and opening it moves that issue's accepted comments to editing. Before its preview is staged, the author writes the change set's Disposition (change set) on the Agent tab: one line per comment (No. 136: Accepted. ...), starting from each comment's Blue Disposition on Review Public Comments, after an optional Overall statement. Quality check: every comment number in the change set has a disposition; the sheet flags gaps and words that differ from the people's (owner, 2026-10-31)."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/public-comment.bpmn:110
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "public-comment import / import-narrative: one record per row or cited passage, anchored through review-anchors.json. Status: received. When the review is also kept in a shared Google Sheet, build its Apps Script with Tool review-sheet-sync (from review/public-comment/sheet-sync.json) and have the sheet's owner install it once (Extensions, Apps Script, run installTriggers): the sheet then keeps its page, section, line and comment links and its change-set joins current by itself."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/public-comment.bpmn:203
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "public-comment incorporate, naming the branch, PR and staging URL; done by the folio's workflow when the PR that closes a change-set issue merges. A PR closed unmerged moves nothing. Ready for merge is set only once the QA gate has passed for the PR's head commit; set earlier, the agent does not merge until it passes. The change set's Dispositions blurb, as it stands when Ready for merge is set to Yes, is the summary that closes its issue (owner, 2026-10-31)."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/public-comment.bpmn:117
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "public-comment triage / reassign / duplicate. An unplaced or low-confidence anchor is placed here, by a person."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/public-comment.bpmn:224
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "public-comment withdraw, from any open status."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/public-comment.bpmn:144
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "public-comment-changesets reroute, or cs-committee: <TWG> — <why> on GitHub from a person in the committee or editor lane (bean se3i, issue #197). Moves the change-set to another TWG review committee and records who, when, from, to and why on the change-set record, so re-ingesting comments never resets it. Person-only (userTask): agents cannot re-route a change-set on their own."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/public-comment.bpmn:132
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "public-comment-changesets seed / propose: the agent groups the comments to be weighed into change-sets, one per change the document may need, each a record under changesets/ with its requirements and members. A PROPOSAL: nothing is decided, no GitHub issue is opened, and a comment may sit in zero, one or several change-sets. The record is the only one; everything shown about a change-set is rendered from it."
msgstr ""

